WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.699 --> 00:00:02.634
-Now, Major League Baseball
just started.

00:00:02.634 --> 00:00:04.133
And in honor of that,
Tariq and I had

00:00:04.133 --> 00:00:06.300
a friendly competition
of our own.

00:00:06.300 --> 00:00:07.601
Look at how friendly he is.

00:00:07.601 --> 00:00:10.334
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:10.334 --> 00:00:13.167
To see who can make
the best baseball-themed cake.

00:00:13.167 --> 00:00:14.567
-Oh.

00:00:14.567 --> 00:00:16.601
It's the first annual
"Tonight Show Cake-Off."

00:00:16.601 --> 00:00:18.133
Now, the rules are simple --

00:00:18.133 --> 00:00:20.267
you have 30 minutes
to decorate your cake

00:00:20.267 --> 00:00:22.400
in the baseball theme
of your choosing,

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:26.300
but no references to teams from
New York or Philadelphia, okay?

00:00:26.300 --> 00:00:28.701
Higgins will judge
who made the best cake

00:00:28.701 --> 00:00:31.267
and declare one of us
the Cake-Off Champion.

00:00:31.267 --> 00:00:32.567
[ Audience cheers ]

00:00:32.567 --> 00:00:34.601
Well, earlier today,
Tariq and I made our cakes,

00:00:34.601 --> 00:00:37.367
and we recorded the whole thing,
which we're about to show you.

00:00:37.367 --> 00:00:40.767
But first, to ensure that it's
a fair and unbiased contest,

00:00:40.767 --> 00:00:44.834
Higgins, please leave the studio
and head to the isolation room.

00:00:44.834 --> 00:00:47.834
-I shall head
to the isolation room.

00:00:47.834 --> 00:00:49.000
[ Laughter ]
-Okay, Higgins, be careful.

00:00:49.000 --> 00:00:50.300
-Ooh!
[ Light jazz music plays ]

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:52.434
-There you go.
That's the isolation room.

00:00:52.434 --> 00:00:55.467
Now, Higgins, please put on
the dome of silence.

00:00:55.467 --> 00:00:58.334
-The dome of silence.
[ Light laughter ]

00:00:58.334 --> 00:01:00.100
-Perfect. All right.

00:01:00.100 --> 00:01:01.934
♪♪

00:01:01.934 --> 00:01:03.200
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.200 --> 00:01:04.467
Here --
[ Light laughter ]

00:01:04.467 --> 00:01:07.567
Here's Tariq and I
earlier today, making our cakes.

00:01:07.567 --> 00:01:08.634
Check it out.

00:01:08.634 --> 00:01:09.934
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:09.934 --> 00:01:15.567
♪♪

00:01:15.567 --> 00:01:16.801
Hi, I'm Jimmy Fallon,

00:01:16.801 --> 00:01:19.167
and this is
my baseball-themed cake.

00:01:19.167 --> 00:01:21.067
I am going to make the head

00:01:21.067 --> 00:01:23.501
of one of my favorite
third basemen of all time,

00:01:23.501 --> 00:01:25.000
Brooks Robinson.

00:01:25.000 --> 00:01:29.000
And I was actually lucky enough
to meet him as a kid --

00:01:29.000 --> 00:01:30.400
I was probably 8 or 9.

00:01:30.400 --> 00:01:32.267
He was nice enough
to even take a photo with me.

00:01:32.267 --> 00:01:33.501
I always loved him.

00:01:33.501 --> 00:01:35.033
-The champ is here.

00:01:35.033 --> 00:01:37.601
I decided to do a carrot cake.

00:01:37.601 --> 00:01:41.267
The brown is sort of comparable
to the soil of the field.

00:01:41.267 --> 00:01:42.400
[ Chuckles ]

00:01:42.400 --> 00:01:43.701
-Tariq doesn't even
watch baseball.

00:01:43.701 --> 00:01:45.601
I don't think Tariq
watches sports.

00:01:45.601 --> 00:01:47.701
-I like baseball.
I like it enough.

00:01:47.701 --> 00:01:49.801
I don't love it.
I love cake.

00:01:49.801 --> 00:01:51.701
-This should be
a home run for me.

00:01:51.701 --> 00:01:52.801
Pun intended.

00:01:52.801 --> 00:01:53.834
Alright,
so what you're gonna do is --

00:01:53.834 --> 00:01:55.968
this is a seven-layer cake.

00:01:55.968 --> 00:01:58.067
So, the first layer goes on.

00:01:58.067 --> 00:01:59.534
Then you want
to put buttercream on.

00:01:59.534 --> 00:02:03.534
-I like to do a cream-cheese
icing with a little carrot top.

00:02:03.534 --> 00:02:06.100
Try and get it as seamless
as possible.

00:02:06.100 --> 00:02:07.267
Yeah, that's pretty good.

00:02:07.267 --> 00:02:08.767
-Now, as I'm going,

00:02:08.767 --> 00:02:11.501
you can kind of see already
the shape of the head.

00:02:11.501 --> 00:02:14.033
Cake and baseball --
it's like, you know --

00:02:14.033 --> 00:02:16.200
The original lyrics of
"Take Me Out to the Ball Game"

00:02:16.200 --> 00:02:17.334
was like...

00:02:17.334 --> 00:02:18.767
♪ Buy me some cake ♪

00:02:18.767 --> 00:02:22.000
-This is my first time
ever hearing cake and baseball

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:23.033
in the same sentence.

00:02:23.033 --> 00:02:24.200
I feel like this is a setup.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:25.467
Like, "Here's the competition --

00:02:25.467 --> 00:02:27.934
we're gonna do, you know,
spaghetti and tennis."

00:02:27.934 --> 00:02:29.067
It's [bleep] stupid.

00:02:29.067 --> 00:02:30.667
It's stupid.
[ Laughter ]

00:02:30.667 --> 00:02:32.667
-It almost looks
exactly like him already.

00:02:32.667 --> 00:02:34.400
Tariq, you're going down, buddy.

00:02:34.400 --> 00:02:37.300
-We can take, like,
a candy popcorn ball,

00:02:37.300 --> 00:02:40.501
and we can cover it
in the fondant

00:02:40.501 --> 00:02:42.167
and make it look
like a baseball.

00:02:42.167 --> 00:02:44.334
-You want to get
some eye holes in there.

00:02:44.334 --> 00:02:46.767
[ Light laughter ]
Stick it in the eye hole.

00:02:46.767 --> 00:02:48.767
It's almost like he's cocking
his head to the side,

00:02:48.767 --> 00:02:52.067
kind of thinking, like,
"Should I catch this one?"

00:02:52.067 --> 00:02:55.467
Now you start applying the skin
so people think

00:02:55.467 --> 00:02:59.400
they are looking at a --
well, a human head.

00:02:59.400 --> 00:03:01.367
Just to even own
"The Tonight Show"

00:03:01.367 --> 00:03:04.667
Championship Bake-Off
golden cake pan would be enough.

00:03:04.667 --> 00:03:06.667
But to have my name
engraved in it?

00:03:06.667 --> 00:03:08.434
That's the icing on the cake.

00:03:08.434 --> 00:03:10.267
-To get my name engraved,

00:03:10.267 --> 00:03:12.234
it would mean
absolutely nothing to me.

00:03:12.234 --> 00:03:14.634
[ Laughter ]
-I had our great Art Department

00:03:14.634 --> 00:03:16.300
help me with the hat.

00:03:16.300 --> 00:03:18.300
You throw a couple skewers
in there

00:03:18.300 --> 00:03:20.968
to help stabilize the hat.

00:03:20.968 --> 00:03:22.400
-Oh!
-Oh!

00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:24.501
-It's all good.
It's all good.

00:03:24.501 --> 00:03:27.601
[ Light laughter ]

00:03:27.601 --> 00:03:30.133
Oh, no. Ohh, God.

00:03:30.133 --> 00:03:31.534
Kind of a disaster.

00:03:31.534 --> 00:03:34.234
All right. Hold on.

00:03:34.234 --> 00:03:36.567
[ Chuckles ]
It's fixable.

00:03:36.567 --> 00:03:38.467
Oh, my gosh.

00:03:38.467 --> 00:03:39.868
[ Laughter ]

00:03:39.868 --> 00:03:42.801
Ah! Don't -- Don't give up.
Don't give up.

00:03:42.801 --> 00:03:44.868
Don't give up.
It's all savable.

00:03:44.868 --> 00:03:46.300
-And then, you know,
you can go in

00:03:46.300 --> 00:03:49.267
and do some baseball-y
sort of details,

00:03:49.267 --> 00:03:51.400
make it look more realistic.

00:03:51.400 --> 00:03:53.000
-So, now that
you got the brim on...

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.501
[ Laughter ]

00:03:55.501 --> 00:03:56.734
Oh, my God!

00:03:56.734 --> 00:03:59.167
So, let's stick a nose on there.

00:03:59.167 --> 00:04:02.667
[ Laughter ]

00:04:02.667 --> 00:04:04.701
Get the eyes, of course.

00:04:04.701 --> 00:04:06.234
You can kind of see it already.

00:04:06.234 --> 00:04:08.467
It's all fixable,
and we can clear it up.

00:04:08.467 --> 00:04:12.834
How confident am I
or how "con-fondant" am I

00:04:12.834 --> 00:04:14.734
that Higgins
will choose my cake?

00:04:14.734 --> 00:04:17.033
He knows Brooks -- he'll take
one look at the cake and go,

00:04:17.033 --> 00:04:18.968
"That's the greatest
third baseman

00:04:18.968 --> 00:04:20.801
in the history of the sport."

00:04:20.801 --> 00:04:23.601
If not, then he's out!

00:04:23.601 --> 00:04:25.300
-If he's judging on just,
you know,

00:04:25.300 --> 00:04:29.868
the most magnificent idea,
then it's already in the bag.

00:04:29.868 --> 00:04:32.834
-If I mush -- If I mess around
with the photo a little bit,

00:04:32.834 --> 00:04:35.200
you can kind of see
where it's going.

00:04:35.200 --> 00:04:36.968
Brooks Robinson.

00:04:36.968 --> 00:04:39.100
-It's going to be spectacular.

00:04:39.100 --> 00:04:40.634
♪♪

00:04:40.634 --> 00:04:42.467
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:42.467 --> 00:04:45.067
[ Laughter ]

00:04:45.067 --> 00:04:46.868
[ Laughter continues ]

00:04:46.868 --> 00:04:51.133
-Dude, it's a disaster.
It's a total disaster!

00:04:51.133 --> 00:04:53.434
Dude, it was looking so good.
It happened so fast.

00:04:53.434 --> 00:04:55.100
It happened
in like three seconds.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:56.701
I'm like, "Oh, my gosh."
-Yup.

00:04:56.701 --> 00:04:57.834
-I got to really sell --

00:04:57.834 --> 00:04:59.667
I got to really sell Higgins
on this one.

00:04:59.667 --> 00:05:01.501
[ Laughter ]
This -- It --

00:05:01.501 --> 00:05:03.033
[ Clears throat ]
Alright. Here we go.

00:05:03.033 --> 00:05:04.467
Tough competition.

00:05:04.467 --> 00:05:07.133
[ Laughter ]

00:05:07.133 --> 00:05:09.801
Higgins may now exit
the isolation room.

00:05:09.801 --> 00:05:11.501
I got to have a poker face.

00:05:11.501 --> 00:05:12.667
[ Breathes sharply ]
[ Laughter ]

00:05:12.667 --> 00:05:13.868
Oh, my gosh.

00:05:13.868 --> 00:05:16.334
Alright.
They poked him...

00:05:16.334 --> 00:05:19.968
And now he can take his place
at the judge's table.

00:05:19.968 --> 00:05:21.634
Higgins.
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:05:21.634 --> 00:05:23.334
There he is, Steve Higgins,
ladies and gentlemen.

00:05:23.334 --> 00:05:26.000
Looking good, bud. Good.
Yeah, this is good.

00:05:26.000 --> 00:05:30.834
Now, Higgins, it is now time
to try the cakes.

00:05:30.834 --> 00:05:34.968
So, whenever you're ready,
please try cake number one.

00:05:34.968 --> 00:05:36.968
-Number one.
-Yes.

00:05:36.968 --> 00:05:39.834
-Ooh, beautiful!
-Uh-huh. Mm-hmm, mm-hmm.

00:05:39.834 --> 00:05:42.834
-Wow!
Looks like a baseball on top.

00:05:42.834 --> 00:05:45.601
-Yep.
-Carrot cake, it looks like.

00:05:45.601 --> 00:05:47.701
There we go. Mmm.
-Nice slice.

00:05:47.701 --> 00:05:50.400
-Okay. Mmm, mmm!

00:05:50.400 --> 00:05:51.868
Mmm!

00:05:51.868 --> 00:05:53.133
♪♪

00:05:53.133 --> 00:05:56.033
-Wow.
-Mmm!

00:05:56.033 --> 00:05:59.534
Mmm.
I'm sensing carrots.

00:05:59.534 --> 00:06:00.868
[ Laughter ]

00:06:00.868 --> 00:06:02.400
-Yeah, well, it's carrot cake.
Yes, of course.

00:06:02.400 --> 00:06:03.501
-And cake.

00:06:03.501 --> 00:06:04.701
-Now Higgins, try...
-Very good.

00:06:04.701 --> 00:06:06.734
Moist, delicious.

00:06:06.734 --> 00:06:08.667
-...cake number two.
-Cake number two.

00:06:08.667 --> 00:06:10.033
-Yeah, there we go.

00:06:10.033 --> 00:06:12.200
[ Laughter ]

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:13.901
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:06:13.901 --> 00:06:15.400
There it is.

00:06:15.400 --> 00:06:16.834
[ Laughter ]

00:06:16.834 --> 00:06:18.767
Cake number two.
-Is that a human ear?

00:06:18.767 --> 00:06:21.801
-That is -- What?
-Oh, my God.

00:06:21.801 --> 00:06:24.234
-[ Laughing ] I have no idea.
-Did the cake drop?

00:06:24.234 --> 00:06:27.567
-What are you talking about?
-Mmm. No, looks delicious.

00:06:27.567 --> 00:06:31.367
-Can you guess --
Can you guess who that is?

00:06:31.367 --> 00:06:34.200
-I'm going to say it's a player
who died in a horrible accident.

00:06:34.200 --> 00:06:36.901
[ Laughter ]
-The famous -- Right?

00:06:36.901 --> 00:06:38.834
-It's the famous player
from the -- from the --

00:06:38.834 --> 00:06:40.267
what -- Baltimore --
is that?

00:06:40.267 --> 00:06:41.434
-That's correct.
-Orioles?

00:06:41.434 --> 00:06:43.033
-Sure.
-Okay, let me try.

00:06:43.033 --> 00:06:45.133
[ Laughs ] Where do --
Where do I even begin

00:06:45.133 --> 00:06:46.868
with this deliciousness?
-That's exactly right.

00:06:46.868 --> 00:06:49.501
-I'm going to say it's
a yellow cake -- I'm guessing.

00:06:49.501 --> 00:06:51.601
-Yup, that's the fun thing
about this cake.

00:06:51.601 --> 00:06:53.167
Everyone can cut it
from all angles.

00:06:53.167 --> 00:06:54.367
-You know what? Yeah.

00:06:54.367 --> 00:06:56.234
And the person becomes
co-author of the cake.

00:06:56.234 --> 00:06:57.834
-You can --
You can remove the hat, too,

00:06:57.834 --> 00:06:59.167
if you want,
and slice down the middle.

00:06:59.167 --> 00:07:00.300
-Oh, let me see
what's underneath there.

00:07:00.300 --> 00:07:01.901
Is it a human brain?
[ Laughter ]

00:07:01.901 --> 00:07:04.367
-It's not a brain.
It's not a brain.

00:07:04.367 --> 00:07:06.300
You can just slice
down the middle.

00:07:06.300 --> 00:07:08.367
[ Laughter ]
-[ Chuckling ]

00:07:08.367 --> 00:07:10.634
-Just get yourself a good slice.
-I got --

00:07:10.634 --> 00:07:12.501
-Wait a second.
There's a spoon in here!

00:07:12.501 --> 00:07:14.200
-Yeah, I was --
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:14.200 --> 00:07:17.634
-I -- Well, you got to make sure
the -- the head was ---

00:07:17.634 --> 00:07:19.334
you got to make sure
the head's sturdy.

00:07:19.334 --> 00:07:22.334
-[ Laughing ] Oh, my God!
-Seriously --

00:07:22.334 --> 00:07:23.767
But th--
Watch out for the skewers.

00:07:23.767 --> 00:07:25.534
-Yeah, there's a lot of --
-Watch out for the --

00:07:25.534 --> 00:07:27.534
There's a little --
Watch out for the skewers.

00:07:27.534 --> 00:07:29.534
-It's like a sauté cake.
-They are not edible.

00:07:29.534 --> 00:07:31.067
The skewers are not edible.
-Yeah, they're not edible.

00:07:31.067 --> 00:07:33.701
-No.
-They are scaffolding.

00:07:33.701 --> 00:07:35.834
-Yeah, to hold it up.
Alright, I'm gonna taste a...

00:07:35.834 --> 00:07:37.701
-All right, here we go.
-...delicious piece of this --

00:07:37.701 --> 00:07:39.567
what I'm going to call "cake."
-[ Laughs ]

00:07:39.567 --> 00:07:42.434
Yeah, that is -- There you go.

00:07:42.434 --> 00:07:44.234
-Okay.
-Yep.

00:07:44.234 --> 00:07:45.767
♪♪

00:07:45.767 --> 00:07:47.100
[ Laughter ]

00:07:47.100 --> 00:07:48.567
Yes, I feel like --
-Mmm!

00:07:48.567 --> 00:07:51.701
-I feel like it's rigged.
-[ Laughing ] So good!

00:07:51.701 --> 00:07:53.200
Wait, I've got
to make sure the hat --

00:07:53.200 --> 00:07:55.267
-Put the hat back on.
-Beautiful. My God.

00:07:55.267 --> 00:07:58.801
That's like -- that's like
a Cake Boss made this one.

00:07:58.801 --> 00:08:00.267
-Yeah. That was a --
[ Laughter ]

00:08:00.267 --> 00:08:02.534
-That's not fair. I mean, you
had a professional who --

00:08:02.534 --> 00:08:03.834
That's that guy I love.

00:08:03.834 --> 00:08:05.200
-Brooks Robinson.
-Brooks --

00:08:05.200 --> 00:08:06.567
[ Laughter ]

00:08:06.567 --> 00:08:08.334
The world-famous
Brooks Robinson,

00:08:08.334 --> 00:08:09.868
my favorite player...
-That's right.

00:08:09.868 --> 00:08:11.167
-...from
the Baltimore Orioles...

00:08:11.167 --> 00:08:12.467
-Yep.
-...who played --

00:08:12.467 --> 00:08:14.300
-It could also be -- It could be
Cal Ripken, if you want.

00:08:14.300 --> 00:08:15.834
-Sure.
-But, no, that's --

00:08:15.834 --> 00:08:16.901
I mean, that's not even funny.

00:08:16.901 --> 00:08:18.534
-Oh, my God. That's beautiful.
-Alright.

00:08:18.534 --> 00:08:20.667
Well, anyways, Higgins,
it's time for your vote.

00:08:20.667 --> 00:08:22.167
[ Drum roll ]

00:08:22.167 --> 00:08:23.601
[ Laughter ]

00:08:23.601 --> 00:08:27.834
Please -- Please write down your
choice for the winning cake...

00:08:27.834 --> 00:08:28.834
-Okay, I'm writing down
my choices,

00:08:28.834 --> 00:08:30.267
putting it in the...

00:08:30.267 --> 00:08:31.534
-...and put it into the official
"Tonight Show Cake-Off"

00:08:31.534 --> 00:08:33.167
ballot box.
-...super secret ballot box.

00:08:33.167 --> 00:08:37.234
-Will it be cake number one
or cake number two?

00:08:37.234 --> 00:08:38.701
♪♪

00:08:38.701 --> 00:08:39.934
-Okay, ready?
I got to unlock it.

00:08:39.934 --> 00:08:41.167
-The vote is locked in.

00:08:41.167 --> 00:08:42.634
-[ Chuckling ] I got to --
I got to unlock it.

00:08:42.634 --> 00:08:44.033
-Alright.
There you go. Yeah.

00:08:44.033 --> 00:08:46.234
I don't know why we have a pad--
Why do we have padlock on there?

00:08:46.234 --> 00:08:47.300
-Ready?

00:08:47.300 --> 00:08:49.334
[ Drum roll ]
-Here we go.

00:08:49.334 --> 00:08:52.667
-The winner is...
-Higgins, the winner is...

00:08:52.667 --> 00:08:54.033
-...cake number one.
-Ah!

00:08:54.033 --> 00:08:55.701
-...cake number one.
Oh, my gosh.

00:08:55.701 --> 00:08:57.234
[ Cheers and applause ]
[ Bell ringing ]

00:08:57.234 --> 00:08:58.901
♪♪

00:08:58.901 --> 00:09:00.133
[ Cheers and applause continue ]

00:09:00.133 --> 00:09:01.334
-Who made --
-Congratulations.

00:09:01.334 --> 00:09:02.767
-Wait, but who made each --
Who made the --

00:09:02.767 --> 00:09:04.834
I don't know who made each cake.
-Tariq.

00:09:04.834 --> 00:09:06.367
Congratulations to

00:09:06.367 --> 00:09:08.701
"The Tonight Show Cake-Off"
winner,

00:09:08.701 --> 00:09:10.200
Tariq Trotter!
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:10.200 --> 00:09:11.801
Tariq Trotter, everybody!
-Alright!

00:09:11.801 --> 00:09:13.000
-Congratulations.
-I just want to --

00:09:13.000 --> 00:09:15.801
I just want to say to
every root vegetable,

00:09:15.801 --> 00:09:18.367
you know, who's been told
to just jump into the juicer

00:09:18.367 --> 00:09:22.267
that you, too, can exist
in a Black Thought cake!

00:09:22.267 --> 00:09:24.067
I mean, I'm talking --
Come on, man.

00:09:24.067 --> 00:09:25.367
[ Cheers and applause ]
-Congratulations

00:09:25.367 --> 00:09:26.868
to "The Tonight Show Cake-Off"
champion, Tariq Trotter.

00:09:26.868 --> 00:09:28.400
-And radishes, beets!
Stick around

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:29.567
for more "Tonight Show,"
everybody!

00:09:29.567 --> 00:09:31.167
-Parsnips!
-Brooks, I'm sorry. I tried.

00:09:31.167 --> 00:09:32.434
-We won!

00:09:32.434 --> 00:09:35.501
Philly! We're taking it
back to Philly, baby!

00:09:35.501 --> 00:09:38.033
Yes, sir! Yes, sir!

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:39.367
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:09:39.367 --> 00:09:44.801
♪♪

